      "key": "abstra",
      "label": "Abstract",
      "searchable": true,
      "value": "AFL-CIO Civil Rights Department, Southeastern Office records (1969-1983) consist of press releases, educational materials, publications, and correspondence. Shortly after the merger in 1955, the AFL-CIO set up a Civil Rights Department, which was designed"
    },
    {
      "controlledVocab": false,
      "controlledVocabList": null,
      "key": "descri",
      "label": "Description",
      "searchable": true,
      "value": "Consists of correspondence regarding the A. Philip Randolph Institute (APRI) Southern Regional Leadership Conferences of 1982 and 1983, the APRI National Conference, regional AFL-CIO conferences, and the 1983 APRI Western Regional Educational Conference, as well as Black History Month, elections, voting, lobbying, housing, and other institute business, and a memorial of A. Philip Randolph."
    },
